From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: aperture: don't sync the viewfinder sink to the clock

A live preview should show frames as they arrive. Synced to the clock,
gtk4paintablesink drops every frame that misses the pipeline's small
latency budget (15 ms here); with a software ISP and GL upload on an
Adreno 306 that is almost every frame: ~2 fps shown of a 28 fps camera
("buffer late, dropping"). A plain pipewiresrc ! glimagesink pipeline
goes from 1.9 fps (sync=true) to ~19 fps (sync=false) on the same device.
---
--- a/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
+++ b/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
@@ -254,6 +254,11 @@
             let tee = crate::PipelineTee::new();

             let paintablesink = gst::ElementFactory::make("gtk4paintablesink")
+                // A live preview shows frames as they arrive: synced to the clock the
+                // sink drops every frame that misses the pipeline's small latency
+                // budget, which on slow GPUs (Adreno 306 + software ISP) left ~2 fps
+                // of a 28 fps camera.
+                .property("sync", false)
                 .build()
                 .expect("Missing gst-plugin-gtk4");

